      "subject": "Learning replays store only what they add to their base correlation",
      "body": "Every Learn now replay started from the designated replay's correlation\nand saved the whole result again, about 11 MB per learning window. A\nlearning replay now saves a revision record, its base replay and what it\nmaterialized, and loading integrates them again. The record is kept only\nwhen it reproduces the full correlation exactly; otherwise the full\nstate is saved as before. A missing base, a cycle or a chain deeper than\n64 fails loudly, never a partial correlation. Checked against the 35\nexisting learning replays: identical on load, 395.9 MB to 0.6 MB.\n\nMission: MS-2026-0010\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AHtXdN7VRusNxTFHzk5uFe",
